simple_sms_native — retained third-party source

The Android MMS implementation contains Kotlin ports and adaptations of
android-smsmms by Jacob Klinker and the Android Open Source Project (AOSP)
MMS stack vendored by that library. These are derived implementations,
not merely references or inspiration. Moving the classes to the plugin's
namespace and translating them to Kotlin does not change their license.

Upstream android-smsmms:
https://github.com/klinker41/android-smsmms

Retained components under android/src/main/kotlin/io/simplezen/simple_sms/:

- mms/sending/: android-smsmms message, transaction, SMS-manager, broadcast,
  settings, status-receiver, utility, and accent-transliteration code.
- mms/codec/: the AOSP-derived MMS PDU composer, parser, model, header,
  character-set, Base64, and quoted-printable code carried by android-smsmms.
- mms/storage/: the PDU persister's cache, SQLite, and DRM helpers carried
  by android-smsmms.
- mms/support/: the retained logging, subscription-column, and download
  constant helpers carried by android-smsmms/AOSP.
- mms/: the content-type definitions, MMS part holder, and exception types.

